FUNCTIONAL COOKIE NAMES

This package also bundles a list of functional cookie names, compiled from the
Open Cookie Database.

    Source:  https://github.com/jkwakman/Open-Cookie-Database
    File:    open-cookie-database.csv, at the commit data/likely-functional-cookies.json
             records in its `sources`
    License: Apache License, Version 2.0
             http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The database's repository carries the standard text of the license, with no copyright
line, and no NOTICE file (checked at each compile, which stops if either appears). The
text of the Apache License 2.0 is LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt at the root of this repository,
and a built extension carries a copy of it at the same path beside its manifest.

WHAT WAS CHANGED

  * data/likely-functional-cookies.json is NOT the database as published. It is a
    derivative: filtered to the entries of infrastructure providers (load balancers,
    bot protection), with entries dropped and names added by this project. The file says
    so in its `modified` field, and each entry names where it came from: the database's
    entry, or the provider's own page for a name this project added.
  * It holds names, categories and providers only. The database's descriptions are not
    included.
  * src/functional-overlay.ts holds what this project decided: which providers are
    taken, which entries are dropped, which names are added, each with its reason. It is
    this project's own work, under GPL-3.0-only.
  * The data file is Apache-2.0, and not covered by the Creative Commons license above. The
    non-commercial term that data puts on the shipped extension does not come from this
    file.


CONTAINER OWNERS' COOKIE NAMES

A second file is compiled from the same database, at the same commit, with the same
license checks: the cookie names each tag manager's owner writes.

    Source:  https://github.com/jkwakman/Open-Cookie-Database
    File:    open-cookie-database.csv, at the commit data/container-owner-cookies.json
             records in its `sources`
    License: Apache License, Version 2.0
             http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

WHAT WAS CHANGED

  * data/container-owner-cookies.json is NOT the database as published. It is a
    derivative: filtered to the names written by the libraries of the companies that own
    each tag manager (Google, Adobe, Matomo, Piwik PRO, Commanders Act, CHEQ), with names
    added by this project from each provider's own documentation (Tealium, Segment, and
    a few Google and Adobe names the database lacks). The file says so in its `modified`
    field, and each entry names where it came from.
  * It holds names, owners and categories only, the categories mapped to this project's
    (the database's Analytics to analytics, Marketing to advertising, any other to
    unknown). The database's descriptions are not included.
  * src/owner-overlay.ts holds what this project decided: the owner of each manager,
    which names are taken and which are added, each with its reason. It is this
    project's own work, under GPL-3.0-only.
  * The data file is Apache-2.0, and not covered by the Creative Commons license above.


PUBLIC SUFFIX LIST

This package also bundles the Public Suffix List, which decides a host's registrable
domain (the site it belongs to) and which domains no site can set a cookie on.

    Source:  https://publicsuffix.org/list/public_suffix_list.dat
    Files:   data/public_suffix_list.dat, as published, at the version and commit it
             records; data/public-suffix-list.json, compiled from it
    License: Mozilla Public License, Version 2.0
             https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/

The list's own license notice, reproduced verbatim from its header:

    This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
    License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
    file, You can obtain one at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.

The text of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 is LICENSES/MPL-2.0.txt at the root of this
repository, and a built extension carries a copy of it at the same path beside its
manifest.

WHAT WAS CHANGED

  * data/public-suffix-list.json holds every rule of the list, in both its sections, and
    nothing else: the comments are dropped, and a rule written in Unicode is converted to
    the ASCII form a hostname arrives in. It carries the list's version, commit and license
    notice. scripts/compile-public-suffix.mjs is the conversion, under GPL-3.0-only.
  * The data files are MPL-2.0, and not covered by the Creative Commons license above.

